或者如果你当时在看某个网站，

774
00:31:08.680 --> 00:31:11.260
there were certain things that we were allowed to show on computer screens,
有些东西是我们被允许在电脑屏幕上展示的，

775
00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:15.200
like fake documents, the Dunder Mifflin logo, free cell games.
比如伪造的文件、邓德·米夫林的标志、空当接龙游戏。

776
00:31:15.280 --> 00:31:16.360
I guess we got that cleared.
我想那些是经过审核的。

777
00:31:17.160 --> 00:31:18.800
But we couldn't have other stuff.
但我们不能放其他东西。

778
00:31:18.800 --> 00:31:19.940
And we would get yelled at.
否则我们会被训斥。

779
00:31:20.100 --> 00:31:24.960
And then Rain said, you never have to tell me again about the screens.
然后雷恩说，你们再也不用提醒我关于屏幕的事了。

780
00:31:25.140 --> 00:31:25.460
All right?
好吗？

781
00:31:25.460 --> 00:31:27.160
Wait, stop hounding me about the screens.
等等，别再为了屏幕的事烦我了。

782
00:31:27.320 --> 00:31:32.700
In fact, if you ever find something on my screen while we're shooting that's not allowed to be
事实上，如果拍摄时你们发现我的屏幕上有任何不允许出现的东西，

783
00:31:32.700 --> 00:31:36.140
there, I will donate $100 to charity every time.
我每次都会捐100美元给慈善机构。

784
00:31:36.280 --> 00:31:38.000
Why was he so annoyed?
他为什么那么烦躁？

785
00:31:38.260 --> 00:31:38.760
I don't know.
我不知道。

786
00:31:38.780 --> 00:31:40.120
He had such a bee in his bonnet.
他当时真是耿耿于怀。

787
00:31:40.220 --> 00:31:43.400
He had to pay out so much because he would forget.
他不得不赔出很多钱，因为他总是会忘。

788
00:31:43.920 --> 00:31:45.560
Oh, and the camera guys would hold him to it.
噢，而且摄影师们会严格执行他的承诺。

789
00:31:45.600 --> 00:31:47.840
Yes, because he made this big declaration.
是的，因为他当时信誓旦旦地宣布了。

790
00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:48.580
Well, good for them.
嗯，他们做得好。

791
00:31:48.600 --> 00:31:50.160
You never need to tell me again.
你们再也不需要提醒我了。

792
00:31:50.160 --> 00:31:56.180
And water bottles, we used to get in trouble for having soda cans or whatever on our desks.
还有水瓶，我们以前因为桌上放着汽水罐之类的东西也会惹麻烦。

793
00:31:56.220 --> 00:32:00.080
I mean, you don't watch Game of Thrones, but there was a Starbucks coffee cup that really—
我是说，你不看《权力的游戏》，但当时有个星巴克咖啡杯真的——

794
00:32:00.080 --> 00:32:04.580
I don't watch Game of Thrones, and yet I did get into the coffee gate situation.
我不看《权力的游戏》，但我确实卷入了那个“咖啡门”事件。

795
00:32:04.720 --> 00:32:04.940
Yeah.
没错。

796
00:32:05.060 --> 00:32:06.480
I thought, how in the world?
我在想，这到底是怎么回事？

797
00:32:06.480 --> 00:32:07.540
How did they miss that?
他们是怎么漏掉那个的？

798
00:32:07.700 --> 00:32:11.000
I mean, there's a Starbucks coffee thing next to like a dragon on the ground.
我是说，地上有一只龙旁边放着星巴克咖啡杯。

799
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:12.660
I mean, that's a whole other world.
我的意思是，那是完全不同的世界。

800
00:32:12.820 --> 00:32:14.560
There are not even Starbucks in that world.
那个世界里甚至根本没有星巴克。

801
00:32:14.560 --> 00:32:19.640
At least if we left a Starbucks on our desk, you could be like, well, I guess they went to Starbucks.
至少如果我们把星巴克的杯子留在桌上，你还能说，嗯，我想他们是去星巴克了。

802
00:32:20.000 --> 00:32:20.180
Yeah.
没错。

803
00:32:20.360 --> 00:32:23.980
I just have to say something that, in watching this again, made me laugh out loud,
我得说点什么，重看这一段时，我忍不住笑出了声，

804
00:32:24.000 --> 00:32:27.060
is that Michael is trying to make everyone feel good about the Dundies.
那就是迈克尔正试图让大家对邓迪奖感到高兴。

805
00:32:27.120 --> 00:32:29.520
He's so wounded that people aren't excited.
他因为大家不兴奋而深受伤害。

806
00:32:29.780 --> 00:32:32.060
This clearly means so much to him.
这对他来说显然意义重大。

807
00:32:32.060 --> 00:32:37.220
And he can't believe that no one else shares his enthusiasm for the Dundies and sees how important they are.
他无法相信竟然没人能像他一样对邓迪奖充满热情，也没人能看出这奖项有多重要。

808
00:32:37.260 --> 00:32:41.060
So as a way to try to, like, get them back into it, he says,
所以为了让大家重新投入其中，他说，

809
00:32:41.060 --> 00:32:45.260
Listen, friends and family are invited to the Dundies for the first time.
听着，亲朋好友第一次受邀参加邓迪奖颁奖礼。

810
00:32:45.460 --> 00:32:47.000
For the first time?
第一次？

811
00:32:47.400 --> 00:32:51.110
Doing the Dundies?
举办邓迪奖？

812
00:32:51.230 --> 00:32:53.190
He's never let them bring plus ones?
他以前从不让大家带家属？

813
00:32:53.370 --> 00:32:54.610
I couldn't believe that.
我简直不敢相信。

814
00:32:54.890 --> 00:32:55.870
I was like, what?
我当时心想，什么？

815
00:32:56.210 --> 00:32:58.150
And everyone was like, oh, great.
而大家却说，哦，太棒了。

816
00:32:58.370 --> 00:33:00.330
Everyone is like genuinely happy about it.
每个人看起来都是真心为此感到高兴。

817
00:33:00.530 --> 00:33:00.830
Yes.
是的。

818
00:33:01.010 --> 00:33:02.050
I was like, oh my gosh.
我当时心想，天哪。

819
00:33:02.070 --> 00:33:03.570
It was like employees only?
以前是仅限员工参加吗？

820
00:33:03.970 --> 00:33:04.430
Oh my lord.
我的天呐。

821
00:33:04.430 --> 00:33:10.730
And then later, you realize that no one is paid for, that everyone now, their bill is going to be double.
后来你才会意识到，没人给家属买单，现在每个人的账单都要翻倍了。

822
00:33:10.890 --> 00:33:11.090
Double.
翻倍。

823
00:33:11.090 --> 00:33:12.110
Because they brought a plus one.
因为他们带了家属。

824
00:33:12.110 --> 00:33:13.870
And they wouldn't have probably even brought anyone.
而且他们本来可能根本不会带任何人来。

825
00:33:14.170 --> 00:33:17.590
So now, guys, we are going to move to the Chili's.
好了，伙计们，我们要出发去奇利餐厅了。

826
00:33:17.690 --> 00:33:18.470
Oh, here we go.
哦，开始了。

827
00:33:18.470 --> 00:33:19.410
It's time to go to Chili's.
是时候去奇利餐厅了。

828
00:33:19.490 --> 00:33:19.540
Here we go.
出发吧。

829
00:33:19.670 --> 00:33:23.870
And if we look like we're sweating, it's because it was over 100 degrees when we shot this episode.
如果我们看起来在冒汗，那是因为拍这一集的时候气温超过了100华氏度。

830
00:33:23.970 --> 00:33:27.870
And there was very little air conditioning inside this abandoned restaurant.
而且这家废弃的餐厅里几乎没有空调。

831
00:33:28.170 --> 00:33:29.530
I'm absolutely fine.
我完全没问题。

832
00:33:29.530 --> 00:33:32.470
Because when I'm completely comfortable, everyone is miserable.
因为当我感到完全舒适时，其他人就惨了。

833
00:33:32.770 --> 00:33:33.090
So.
所以。

834
00:33:33.930 --> 00:33:35.810
I was doing okay as well.
我当时也还好。

835
00:33:36.010 --> 00:33:38.410
But the gentlemen, the men wearing suits were.
但那些男士们，穿着西装的男士们就惨了。

836
00:33:38.410 --> 00:33:38.690
Poor.
可怜。

837
00:33:38.730 --> 00:33:39.550
Well, poor Steve.
嗯，可怜的史蒂夫。

838
00:33:39.550 --> 00:33:40.650
In a tuxedo.
穿着燕尾服。

839
00:33:40.930 --> 00:33:43.150
And then he would put things on top of the tuxedo.
然后他还要在燕尾服外面套东西。

840
00:33:43.290 --> 00:33:43.450
Yeah.
没错。

841
00:33:44.010 --> 00:33:44.430
Yeah.
没错。

842
00:33:44.610 --> 00:33:46.950
We spent three full days filming there.
我们在那里整整拍了三天。

843
00:33:47.010 --> 00:33:52.410
And we also had to sometimes wear coats because we were pretending like it was fall.
而且我们有时还得穿外套，因为我们要假装当时是秋天。

844
00:33:52.610 --> 00:33:52.910
Right.
对。

845
00:33:53.030 --> 00:33:55.370
If you see rain, he's got that big trench coat on.
如果你看到下雨的戏，他穿着那件大风衣。

846
00:33:55.630 --> 00:33:57.050
It always worked out that way.
总是这样。

847
00:33:57.130 --> 00:34:02.910
We would film all these episodes that we'll talk about where we were in coats and suits and stuff outside and it was AuguSt.
我们拍的所有这些剧集，我们之后会聊到，当时我们在外面穿着外套和西装，可那会儿是八月。

848
00:34:02.910 --> 00:34:09.730
Or we would have to pretend like it was spring, but we were shooting it during the winter and we would be freezing.
或者我们得假装是春天，但拍摄时正值冬天，我们都快冻僵了。

849
00:34:10.010 --> 00:34:10.290
Yes.
是的。

850
00:34:10.910 --> 00:34:15.890
We never shot the episodes during the time of year in which they were.
我们从来没有在剧集设定的那个季节去拍摄。

851
00:34:16.070 --> 00:34:21.830
I love Oscar's talking head, his description of the Dundies, comparing them to a children's party.
我喜欢奥斯卡的访谈片段，他把邓迪奖比作儿童派对的描述太棒了。

852
00:34:21.970 --> 00:34:23.870
He did that so well.
他演得真好。

853
00:34:23.870 --> 00:34:25.730
It was so spot on.
简直一针见血。

854
00:34:25.850 --> 00:34:27.990
Oscar always has some of my favorite talking heads.
奥斯卡的访谈片段总是我最喜欢的。

855
00:34:28.150 --> 00:34:28.790
He's brilliant.
他太有才了。

856
00:34:28.790 --> 00:34:30.090
He's an amazing actor.
他是一位了不起的演员。

857
00:34:30.330 --> 00:34:30.950
He really is.
确实如此。

858
00:34:30.950 --> 00:34:38.090
Oscar describes the Dundies as a child's birthday party and Pam compares it to an accident that you're forced to look at.
奥斯卡把邓迪奖形容成孩子的生日派对，而帕姆把它比作一场你不得不盯着看的车祸。

859
00:34:38.290 --> 00:34:39.030
You're forced to look at.
不得不盯着看。

860
00:34:39.170 --> 00:34:40.890
I have a question for you, Jenna.
珍娜，我有个问题想问你。

861
00:34:41.070 --> 00:34:41.290
Yeah.
嗯。

862
00:34:41.590 --> 00:34:41.910
All right.
好的。

863
00:34:42.050 --> 00:34:44.670
I read, when I was looking back over the Dundies,
我在回顾邓迪奖那集时读到，

864
00:34:44.850 --> 00:34:55.690
I read an article that said that BJ Novak took Jenna out to get drunk in real life and then let her know what her responses were like because you don't really drink that much in real life.
我读到一篇文章说，现实生活中BJ·诺瓦克带你去喝醉了，然后让你感受一下自己的反应，因为你现实中其实不怎么喝酒。

865
00:34:55.810 --> 00:34:57.410
So he took you out drinking.
所以他带你去喝酒了。

866
00:34:57.450 --> 00:34:58.430
Is that true?
这是真的吗？

867
00:34:58.710 --> 00:34:59.150
Yes.
是的。

868
00:34:59.650 --> 00:35:00.090
What?
什么？

869
00:35:00.330 --> 00:35:00.650
Yes.
是的。

870
00:35:00.950 --> 00:35:04.830
I was nervous about this episode because Pam had to be drunk.
我当时对这一集很紧张，因为帕姆必须表现出醉酒的状态。

871
00:35:05.030 --> 00:35:07.010
And that's hard to play and not be goofy.
要演好醉酒而不显得滑稽是很难的。

872
00:35:07.230 --> 00:35:07.650
It is.
确实。

873
00:35:07.730 --> 00:35:12.370
And I confided in the writers and I said, I'm nervous.
我向编剧们吐露了心声，我说，我很紧张。

874
00:35:12.570 --> 00:35:14.410
I don't know how to do it.
我不知道该怎么演。

875
00:35:14.550 --> 00:35:22.610
And Mindy had a great stage direction later where she was saying, you know, Pam is nodding along.
后来敏迪给了一个很棒的舞台指导，她说，你知道，帕姆在点头附和。

876
00:35:22.710 --> 00:35:23.570
I loved that.
我喜欢那个设计。

877
00:35:23.790 --> 00:35:27.070
That was in the script that Pam is nodding.
剧本里确实写了帕姆在点头。

878
00:35:27.170 --> 00:35:27.310
Right.
没错。

879
00:35:27.310 --> 00:35:28.230
When she's really drunk.
当她喝得很醉的时候。

880
00:35:28.430 --> 00:35:29.330
That you're trying so hard to pay attention.
那种你努力想要集中注意力的样子。

881
00:35:29.530 --> 00:35:29.790
Yes.
是的。

882
00:35:29.790 --> 00:35:30.390
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

883
00:35:30.390 --> 00:35:31.990
I'm a normal person paying attention.
就像一个正常人在努力听讲一样。

884
00:35:32.110 --> 00:35:32.290
Yes.
是的。

885
00:35:32.350 --> 00:35:33.450
Look how I'm nodding at you.
你看我正对着你点头呢。

886
00:35:33.890 --> 00:35:35.650
So that was Mindy's stage direction.
所以那是敏迪的舞台指导。

887
00:35:35.890 --> 00:35:39.550
But the rest of it, like, how do you gradually become drunk?
但剩下的部分，比如，你怎么逐渐变得醉醺醺的？

888
00:35:39.550 --> 00:35:44.950
And I was really afraid that I was going to do just some horrible, fake, drunky performance.
我真的很怕自己会演出一场糟糕、虚假、醉酒式的表演。

889
00:35:45.230 --> 00:35:46.090
You did fantastic.
你演得太棒了。

890
00:35:46.090 --> 00:35:46.310
Fantastic.
非常棒。

891
00:35:46.590 --> 00:35:47.150
Thank you.
谢谢。

892
00:35:47.550 --> 00:35:48.950
So BJ and I get to talking.
所以BJ和我聊了起来。

893
00:35:49.070 --> 00:35:59.410
And we decide, how about we go out, I'll have some drinks, and BJ will ask me questions and help me observe what it feels like to slowly get drunk.
我们决定，不如出去喝几杯，BJ问我一些问题，帮我观察慢慢喝醉是什么感觉。

894
00:35:59.610 --> 00:36:02.250
So he was sort of going to document you having drinks.
所以他算是要记录你喝酒的过程。

895
00:36:02.410 --> 00:36:02.610
Yes.
是的。

896
00:36:02.710 --> 00:36:03.790
This is really method.
这真是体验派演法。

897
00:36:04.030 --> 00:36:04.530
This is super nerdy.
这太书呆子气了。

898
00:36:04.530 --> 00:36:06.030
I like it, though.
不过我喜欢。

899
00:36:06.170 --> 00:36:10.670
And I know why I didn't take you out, because I would have been the one also being like, I'll have drinks, too.
我知道为什么我没带你去了，因为我也会跟着说，我也要喝几杯。

900
00:36:10.790 --> 00:36:12.490
It's like, no, this defeats the purpose.
那样的话，就完全违背初衷了。

901
00:36:12.510 --> 00:36:13.950
This is a scientific experiment.
这是一项科学实验。

902
00:36:14.650 --> 00:36:24.690
So, yeah, so I went out with BJ, and it was really interesting, because after the first two drinks, I was like, oh, I just feel buzzed and a little dizzy.
所以，没错，我和BJ出去约会了，那真的很有趣，因为喝了两杯之后，我就觉得有点微醺，还有点晕乎乎的。

903
00:36:24.690 --> 00:36:30.930
I was laughing a lot, so that's why I had Pam do all of those ridiculous laughs in the episode.
我当时笑个不停，所以这就是为什么我让帕姆在剧集里发出那些荒唐的笑声。

904
00:36:31.130 --> 00:36:32.910
But by drink number four, I—
但喝到第四杯的时候，我——

905
00:36:32.910 --> 00:36:33.570
Four?
四杯？

906
00:36:33.810 --> 00:36:34.590
Number four?
第四杯？

907
00:36:34.730 --> 00:36:37.190
By drink number four, I was drinking Cosmopolitans.
喝到第四杯的时候，我喝的是大都会鸡尾酒。

908
00:36:37.270 --> 00:36:38.150
Oh, my gosh, Jenna.
天哪，珍娜。

909
00:36:38.250 --> 00:36:39.130
Did you get sick?
你喝吐了吗？

910
00:36:39.350 --> 00:36:40.670
I didn't get sick.
我没喝吐。

911
00:36:40.670 --> 00:36:41.610
Oh, good Lord.
天呐，我的老天。

912
00:36:41.770 --> 00:36:42.250
I know.
我知道。

913
00:36:42.250 --> 00:36:47.570
So, by drink number four, apparently, I said to BJ, I don't feel drunk at all.
所以，喝到第四杯时，我显然对BJ说，我一点都没觉得醉。

914
00:36:47.610 --> 00:36:48.230
I feel normal.
我觉得很正常。

915
00:36:49.090 --> 00:36:51.150
And BJ said, really?
BJ说，真的吗？

916
00:36:51.910 --> 00:36:56.170
Because you're talking really loud and really close, and you almost just fell over.
因为你说话声音特别大，离我特别近，而且刚才差点摔倒。

917
00:36:56.550 --> 00:36:57.970
And I was like, I did?
我说，我有吗？

918
00:36:59.070 --> 00:37:01.150
So, I stopped after drink number four.
所以，我在喝完第四杯后就停下了。

919
00:37:01.290 --> 00:37:08.070
But I thought that it was really interesting how, after so many drinks, I doubted that I was even drunk.
但我认为很有趣的一点是，喝了那么多杯之后，我竟然怀疑自己到底有没有醉。

920
00:37:08.430 --> 00:37:08.950
Yes.
是的。

921
00:37:08.950 --> 00:37:13.590
And so, all that information, I kind of weaved into my performance.
所以，我把这些信息都融入到了我的表演中。

922
00:37:14.010 --> 00:37:15.530
Well, it worked, lady.
好吧，这招奏效了，女士。

923
00:37:15.790 --> 00:37:16.290
Thank you.
谢谢。

924
00:37:16.290 --> 00:37:17.850
And I'm glad you didn't have a hangover.
很高兴你没有宿醉。

925
00:37:18.790 --> 00:37:20.730
So, folks, drink responsibly.
所以，各位，请理性饮酒。

926
00:37:21.030 --> 00:37:21.310
Yeah.
没错。

927
00:37:21.630 --> 00:37:22.950
Don't drink four, Cosmos.
别喝四杯大都会鸡尾酒。

928
00:37:23.210 --> 00:37:23.510
Yeah.
没错。

929
00:37:23.770 --> 00:37:25.030
Don't drink four, Cosmos.
别喝四杯大都会鸡尾酒。

930
00:37:25.030 --> 00:37:26.190
We do not recommend.
我们不推荐这样做。

931
00:37:26.610 --> 00:37:31.350
Rain got really into the sound effects on that keyboard.
雷恩在那台键盘上玩音效玩得很起劲。

932
00:37:31.570 --> 00:37:32.050
He did.
确实。

933
00:37:32.250 --> 00:37:32.850
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

934
00:37:32.850 --> 00:37:33.230
I do.
记得。

935
00:37:33.390 --> 00:37:36.930
So, they had a keyboard for him, and they told him the different sounds the keyboard made.
他们给了他一台键盘，并告诉他键盘能发出哪些不同的声音。

936
00:37:37.110 --> 00:37:40.210
This is like handing a child, like, a keyboard.
这就像是给小孩子递了一台键盘一样。

937
00:37:40.470 --> 00:37:42.870
Or it's like, even when you give Rain a microphone.
或者就像你给雷恩一个麦克风一样。

938
00:37:43.050 --> 00:37:43.530
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

939
00:37:43.790 --> 00:37:45.930
Get ready, because he's going to have a lot of bits.
做好准备吧，因为他会有很多即兴表演。

940
00:37:46.090 --> 00:37:50.310
And they told him he could play it whenever he wanted during Michael's speeches.
他们告诉他，在迈克尔演讲的时候，他随时都可以弹奏。

941
00:37:50.430 --> 00:37:51.650
And did he ever.
他确实也这么做了。

942
00:37:51.650 --> 00:37:57.890
Or, I mean, right out of the gate, when Michael's like, well, Stanley, I can't wait to meet your wife.
或者说，刚一开始，当迈克尔说，好吧，斯坦利，我迫不及待想见见你妻子时。

943
00:37:57.970 --> 00:38:00.370
And she's like, I'm holding her hand right now.
而他却说，我现在正牵着她的手呢。

944
00:38:00.710 --> 00:38:04.230
Like, that was Rain improviser, like, brr, brr.
那完全是雷恩的即兴发挥，比如，嘟嘟，嘟嘟。

945
00:38:04.310 --> 00:38:04.590
Yeah.
没错。

946
00:38:04.810 --> 00:38:06.610
That was just Rain having fun on the keyboard.
那只是雷恩在键盘上自娱自乐。

947
00:38:06.890 --> 00:38:10.870
There was also an, oh, yeah, that he used to play.
还有一个他经常弹的“哦，耶”。

948
00:38:11.030 --> 00:38:11.770
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

949
00:38:11.850 --> 00:38:15.090
And Rain kept doing it at the most inappropriate moments.
雷恩总是在最不合时宜的时候弹奏它。

950
00:38:15.130 --> 00:38:18.450
And that was the thing that would make Steve break more than anything else.
那也是最容易让史蒂夫笑场的事情。

951
00:38:18.450 --> 00:38:21.310
It wasn't the fart noise or the trumpet sounds.
那不是放屁声或者小号声。

952
00:38:21.490 --> 00:38:23.470
It was that, oh, yeah, button.
而是那个“哦，耶”按钮。

953
00:38:23.610 --> 00:38:27.350
And there was one time where Steve broke down laughing.
有一次史蒂夫笑得停不下来。

954
00:38:27.350 --> 00:38:28.850
It felt like 10 minutes.
感觉像过了十分钟一样。

955
00:38:28.910 --> 00:38:30.130
He could not get it back.
他怎么也止不住。

956
00:38:30.210 --> 00:38:31.330
He doubled over.
他笑得腰都弯了。

957
00:38:31.510 --> 00:38:35.730
We had to stop filming, because he got so tickled, because Rain kept hitting that, oh, yeah, button.
我们不得不停止拍摄，因为他被逗得太厉害了，雷恩一直在按那个“哦，耶”按钮。

958
00:38:35.910 --> 00:38:37.310
And Steve never breaks.
史蒂夫从不笑场。

959
00:38:37.570 --> 00:38:38.990
He is a rock.
他就像块磐石。

960
00:38:39.090 --> 00:38:40.750
He and Oscar are the two.
他和奥斯卡是唯二的两个。

961
00:38:40.910 --> 00:38:41.190
Oh.
哦。

962
00:38:41.290 --> 00:38:43.030
It is very hard to make either of them break.
要让他们俩笑场非常难。

963
00:38:43.130 --> 00:38:45.410
Oh, I would say they were statues for a long time.
哦，我会说他们俩很长一段时间里就像雕像一样。

964
00:38:45.490 --> 00:38:46.790
I was like, Oscar, are you a robot?
我当时心想，奥斯卡，你是机器人吗？

965
00:38:47.030 --> 00:38:48.230
Let's get into the awards.
我们来聊聊颁奖环节吧。

